  "body": "Two 🟡 findings require changes before merge.\n\n🟡 **Finding 1**: `KanbanBoard.context.tsx` passes `taskSearchQuery` to both `task_id` and `title` params simultaneously. AND semantics means searching \"T1\" returns no results because task titles don't contain \"T1\". Fix: map the single search box to `title` only.\n\n🟡 **Finding 2**: `useBoardData.ts` has a `useEffect` with no dependency array and a `tick === 0` guard that silently drops sync updates after the user clicks Retry. Fix: add `[options.initialData]` dep array and remove `tick === 0` guard.\n\nSee full review narrative in the PR comments.",
  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "src/features/board/components/KanbanBoard/KanbanBoard.context.tsx",
      "line": 133,
      "body": "🟡 **Important** — Dual `task_id`+`title` mapping from single search input.\n\nPassing the same `taskSearchQuery` as both `task_id` and `title` applies AND semantics on the backend. Typing \"T1\" would return zero results because task titles don't contain \"T1\". The spec says these are separate filter controls.\n\n**Fix**: Drop `task_id` from this mapping; use only `title` for the unified search box."
    },
    {
      "path": "src/features/board/hooks/useBoardData.ts",
      "line": 61,
      "body": "🟡 **Important** — `useEffect` without dependency array + `tick === 0` guard.\n\nThis effect runs on every render (no dep array). More critically, the `tick === 0` condition means that after a user clicks Retry (tick becomes 1), workspace sync updates are silently dropped — the board stays stale even after sync completes.\n\n**Fix**: Add `[options.initialData]` to the dependency array and remove the `tick === 0` guard."
    }
  ]
}

